  "notes": [
    "This contract freezes Q2 multimodal train-ready artifacts; it never edits raw data.",
    "Q2 fold-role artifacts are temporal-unit level and are not row-count aligned with window-level X.",
    "Fold event weights retain fold_count x window_count rows and bind the ordered fixed6 selection without entering model X.",
    "Actor and actor-partner visual caches use letterbox padding to preserve bbox aspect ratio.",
    "X artifacts must be checked against explicit whitelist logic, not all numeric columns.",
    "pig_id is an annotation-local identity and must not be treated as a biological identity across videos.",
    "The scientific claim is Q2 internal recording-date/video-safe improvement, not external farm/camera/cohort generalization."
  ]
